A||||11||isthiswhereiputausername?||rusty brake lines?||||5||
Z||000000||isthiswhereiputausername?||06-14-2001||04:05 PM||||Since my car was stored for 3 years and the lines have a little rust on them, I'm thinking of replacing them all front to back..(want the car safe for when my wife drives it)<P>When replacing them with stainless steel lines, are there any specific size of lines I need to replace my old ones with? <P>I will be using the existing blocks the lines go into and creating my own lines using a flange we have at the garage..<P>What size of brake line roll will I need to pick up?<P>Anyone create their own lines ?<P>How much line is needed to replace every line with stainless steel?<P><BR>Thanks<P><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||SteveJ||06-14-2001||07:10 PM||||I used the green coated lines sold by Autozone. Only size I remember is the line from the MC to the Y block behind the passenger rear wheel. I think it was 1/4 inch which was a size larger than all the others.<BR>Your biggest problem is all the bends needed from the proportioning valve out the bottom of the trunk. You need a good tubing bender that does tight bends.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||06-14-2001||07:59 PM||||Stainless lines DO NOT directly replace steel. There are several rules, like different flairing, to be followed and all the fittings will need adapters since you can't get the correct flair on the rubber lines and etc. <P>The biggest difference is that you Do Not double flair SS line. It is too brittle and will fail. It als flairs to a differant angle... about 37 instead of 45 degrees.<P>stay with a good brand of steel line. It will last just fine and you won't have to buy special parts to use it.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 06-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||SteveJ||06-14-2001||08:56 PM||||You know the more I think about this the more pi$$ed I get. Safety concerns and issues everywhere you look. Warnings 'till you get sick of 'em. Yet they still make brake lines that predictably rust out. Isn't that a safety concern? Why not make 'em out of stainless at the factory? <P>For pete sake they make the muffler out of stainless and not the brakes!||||reg||1
Z||000004||SteveJ||06-14-2001||08:57 PM||||. . .and what about the gas lines? Isn't it a fire hazzard to have them rusting out? Environmental issue too?||||reg||1
